{"name":"Light Bathing","hex":"#abd5dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"bathing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of taking a bath.","The act of swimming."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bathe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bathing","blocks":[{"text":"Bathing is the immersion of the body, wholly or partially, usually in water, but often in another medium such as hot air. It is most commonly practised as part of personal cleansing, and less frequently for relaxation or as a leisure activity. Cleansing the body may be solely a component of personal hygiene, but is also a spiritual part of some religious rituals. Bathing is also sometimes used medically or therapeutically, as in hydrotherapy, ice baths, or the mud bath."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Norblin_Bath_in_the_park_%28detail%29_02.jpg/330px-Norblin_Bath_in_the_park_%28detail%29_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathing","wikidata":"Q327651"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/500px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/1280px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/500px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astronaut Jack R. Lousma taking a shower in space, 1973","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShowering_on_Skylab_(9456594881).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg/500px-A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg/1280px-A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg/500px-A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna